Title: rtk: exclude git from the hook rewrite on every machine
Created: 2026-10-09
Author: Minh Ha-Duong

--- log ---
2026-10-09T13:37Z Minh Ha-Duong created

--- body ---
## Context
rtk 0.49.0 rewrites most mutating git subcommands (`add`, `commit`, `push`,
`fetch`, `worktree`, `branch`, `diff`, `show`, `git -C …`) into `rtk git …`.
The worktree isolation guard cannot verify where a wrapped git runs and
refuses it: about eight refusals in the 2026-10-09 roar of PR #1300, each
passing at once as `/usr/bin/git`. Plumbing (`rev-parse`, `merge-base`) and
`switch` are not rewritten. Git is absent from `rtk gain`'s top 10 on doudou
(10th entry 306.5K of 366.9M saved, <0.1 %), so excluding it costs ~nothing.

## Change
`~/.config/rtk/config.toml` `[hooks] exclude_commands`: replace `"git log"`,
`"git status"` with `"^git\\b"` (subsumes both, ticket 0932). Machine-local by
design (0932): not committed; record each machine here.

## Exit criteria
- [x] doudou: config edited 2026-10-09
- [ ] doudou: `rtk hook check "git commit -q -m x"` prints `No rewrite`, and
      `rtk hook check "ls -la"` still rewrites (positive control)
- [ ] padme: same edit, same two checks
- [x] `RTK.md` example no longer shows `git status` → `rtk git status`

